WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.559
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Sarah. Welcome to Online A one, Book three.

2
00:00:05.859 --> 00:00:09.222
Hi! I'm Rithy. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.522 --> 00:00:16.122
Unit twelve: Recycling. In this unit, you will talk about recycling and keeping our planet clean.

4
00:00:17.117 --> 00:00:18.211
Recycle.

5
00:00:18.911 --> 00:00:22.628
Recycle means to use old things again to make new things.

6
00:00:22.928 --> 00:00:24.765
We recycle paper at school.

7
00:00:25.465 --> 00:00:28.640
Your turn. Say: Recycle.

8
00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:32.237
Recycle.

9
00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:34.193
Plastic.

10
00:00:34.893 --> 00:00:38.472
Plastic means a light material used for bottles and bags.

11
00:00:38.772 --> 00:00:40.643
Don't throw plastic in the river.

12
00:00:41.343 --> 00:00:44.112
Your turn. Say: Plastic.

13
00:00:46.812 --> 00:00:47.685
Plastic.

14
00:00:48.683 --> 00:00:49.510
Paper.

15
00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:53.255
Paper means thin material we write on.

16
00:00:53.555 --> 00:00:55.194
Put the paper in the blue bin.

17
00:00:55.894 --> 00:00:58.280
Your turn. Say: Paper.

18
00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:01.737
Paper.

19
00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:03.496
Bottle.

20
00:01:04.196 --> 00:01:07.298
Bottle means a container for water or drinks.

21
00:01:07.598 --> 00:01:09.458
I recycle my water bottle.

22
00:01:10.158 --> 00:01:12.788
Your turn. Say: Bottle.

23
00:01:15.488 --> 00:01:16.233
Bottle.

24
00:01:17.217 --> 00:01:18.009
Can.

25
00:01:18.709 --> 00:01:21.463
Can means a metal container for drinks or food.

26
00:01:21.763 --> 00:01:23.461
This can is made of metal.

27
00:01:24.161 --> 00:01:26.732
Your turn. Say: Can.

28
00:01:29.432 --> 00:01:30.038
Can.

29
00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:31.703
Bin.

30
00:01:32.403 --> 00:01:34.518
Bin means a container for rubbish.

31
00:01:34.818 --> 00:01:36.203
Use the right bin.

32
00:01:36.903 --> 00:01:39.416
Your turn. Say: Bin.

33
00:01:42.116 --> 00:01:42.768
Bin.

34
00:01:43.783 --> 00:01:44.657
Rubbish.

35
00:01:45.357 --> 00:01:47.472
Rubbish means things we throw away.

36
00:01:47.772 --> 00:01:49.400
Pick up the rubbish, please.

37
00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:52.741
Your turn. Say: Rubbish.

38
00:01:55.441 --> 00:01:56.349
Rubbish.

39
00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:58.258
Planet.

40
00:01:58.958 --> 00:02:01.190
Planet means our world, the Earth.

41
00:02:01.490 --> 00:02:03.466
Let's keep our planet clean.

42
00:02:04.166 --> 00:02:06.830
Your turn. Say: Planet.

43
00:02:09.530 --> 00:02:10.299
Planet.

44
00:02:11.283 --> 00:02:13.573
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:13.873 --> 00:02:16.407
Ms. Sarah, what can we recycle?

46
00:02:17.717 --> 00:02:20.808
We can recycle paper, plastic bottles and cans.

47
00:02:22.117 --> 00:02:23.687
Where should we put them?

48
00:02:24.983 --> 00:02:26.867
We should put them in the recycling bin.

49
00:02:28.183 --> 00:02:30.078
Why is recycling important?

50
00:02:31.383 --> 00:02:34.265
It keeps our planet clean and saves trees.

51
00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:38.722
Grammar focus: We can and We should.

52
00:02:39.022 --> 00:02:41.837
We can recycle bottles. We should use a bin.

53
00:02:42.137 --> 00:02:46.194
'Can' tells us what is possible. 'Should' tells us what is a good idea.

54
00:02:47.183 --> 00:02:50.486
Now read and listen. Clean School, Clean Planet.

55
00:02:50.786 --> 00:02:53.122
At our school, we recycle every day.

56
00:02:54.417 --> 00:02:58.030
We can recycle paper, plastic bottles and cans.

57
00:02:59.317 --> 00:03:01.293
We put rubbish in the right bin.

58
00:03:02.583 --> 00:03:05.291
On Friday, we pick up rubbish around the school.

59
00:03:06.583 --> 00:03:09.082
Recycling helps keep our planet clean.

60
00:03:10.383 --> 00:03:13.059
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:15.684
We blank recycle paper and cans.

62
00:03:15.984 --> 00:03:19.300
A, can. B, cans. C, canning.

63
00:03:23.317 --> 00:03:26.129
The answer is A: can.

64
00:03:27.617 --> 00:03:29.628
You blank put rubbish in the bin.

65
00:03:29.928 --> 00:03:33.604
A, should. B, shoulds. C, should to.

66
00:03:37.617 --> 00:03:39.895
The answer is A: should.

67
00:03:41.383 --> 00:03:43.244
Things we throw away are blank.

68
00:03:43.544 --> 00:03:47.487
A, rubbish. B, planets. C, paper.

69
00:03:51.483 --> 00:03:53.425
The answer is A: rubbish.

70
00:03:54.917 --> 00:03:58.405
Now it's your turn to speak. What can you recycle at home?

71
00:04:03.705 --> 00:04:09.422
At home, we can recycle plastic bottles and old paper. We should never throw rubbish in the river.

72
00:04:09.722 --> 00:04:11.501
Excellent answer, Rithy!

73
00:04:12.517 --> 00:04:17.503
Great work today! You learned eight new words and we can and we should.

74
00:04:17.803 --> 00:04:22.998
Today's value is caring for nature. Care for plants, birds and our planet.

75
00:04:23.298 --> 00:04:26.577
See you in Unit thirteen. Goodbye!

76
00:04:26.877 --> 00:04:29.901
Thank you, Ms. Sarah! Bye, everyone!

